{\b\fs24\cf1 ShotTray is ready}\par
{\cf2 It lives in the system tray (bottom-right, next to the clock). If you can't see the blue icon, click the {\b ^} arrow there.}\par
\par
{\b\fs20\cf1 1. Take a screenshot}\par
\bullet  Press {\b Ctrl + Shift + 4}, then drag a box over what you want.\par
\bullet  Or left-click the tray icon.\par
\bullet  {\b Esc} or right-click cancels.\par
\par
{\b\fs20\cf1 2. Use the thumbnail}\par
A small preview slides in at the bottom-right for 6 seconds (hover to keep it).\par
\bullet  {\b Drag} it into a folder, the Desktop, a browser, Discord, Slack, VS Code...\par
\bullet  {\b Click} it to draw on it.\par
\bullet  {\b Right-click} for: Edit, Open, Copy image, Copy path, Save as, Show in folder, Delete.\par
\bullet  Every capture is also {\b copied to the clipboard}, so you can just press {\b Ctrl + V}.\par
\par
{\b\fs20\cf1 3. Mark it up}\par
Click the thumbnail to open the editor:\par
\bullet  {\b P} pen, {\b H} highlighter, {\b A} arrow, {\b R} rectangle, {\b E} ellipse, {\b T} text\par
\bullet  Hold {\b Shift} for a perfect square or circle\par
\bullet  {\b 1 2 3} small / medium / large, {\b Ctrl+Z} / {\b Ctrl+Y} undo / redo\par
\bullet  {\b Enter} or {\b Ctrl+S} = Done (saves and copies), {\b Esc} closes\par
\par
{\b\fs20\cf1 4. Tray menu}\par
Right-click the tray icon: Capture area, Open screenshots folder, Copy last screenshot path, Start with Windows, Exit.\par
\par
{\b\fs20\cf1 5. The shot command}\par
In a {\b new} terminal (if you added it to PATH):\par
\bullet  {\f1 shot} \endash  path of the latest screenshot\par
\bullet  {\f1 shot list 5} \endash  the 5 most recent\par
\bullet  {\f1 shot open} \endash  open the screenshots folder\par
Handy for AI coding tools: run {\f1 shot} and paste the path, or paste the image with {\b Alt+V} in Claude Code.\par
\par
{\b\fs20\cf1 Where are my screenshots?}\par
{\f1 %LOCALAPPDATA%\\ShotTray\\Screenshots} \endash  kept for 7 days, then deleted automatically. Anything you drag or "Save as" elsewhere is a copy and is never deleted.\par
\par
{\cf2 The full guide is always one click away in the Start menu: ShotTray Guide.}\par
